e twelve. The knowledge of scriptures is better than mere ritualistic practice; meditation is better than scriptural knowledge; renunciation of attachment to the fruits of all work is better than meditation; peace immediately follows renunciation.","start":90.456,"at":91.032,"end":111.168,"words":[[0.138,0.237,"Then"],[0.388,0.138,"he"],[0.537,0.362,"ranks"],[0.912,0.1,"the"],[1.025,0.475,"paths"],[1.512,0.138,"in"],[1.663,0.062,"a"],[1.738,0.525,"single"],[2.475,0.625,"surprising"],[3.112,0.55,"verse"],[4.025,0.45,"Verse"],[4.487,0.625,"twelve"],[5.513,0.075,"The"],[5.6,0.35,"knowledge"],[5.963,0.1,"of"],[6.075,0.625,"scriptures"],[6.713,0.175,"is"],[6.9,0.325,"better"],[7.237,0.138,"than"],[7.388,0.263,"mere"],[7.662,0.688,"ritualistic"],[8.363,0.625,"practice"],[9.275,0.625,"meditation"],[9.912,0.125,"is"],[10.05,0.275,"better"],[10.338,0.163,"than"],[10.512,0.512,"scriptural"],[11.037,0.45,"knowledge"],[11.787,0.713,"renunciation"],[12.512,0.087,"of"],[12.613,0.65,"attachment"],[13.275,0.075,"to"],[13.363,0.1,"the"],[13.475,0.35,"fruits"],[13.838,0.1,"of"],[13.95,0.175,"all"],[14.137,0.325,"work"],[14.475,0.138,"is"],[14.625,0.287,"better"],[14.925,0.125,"than"],[15.062,0.725,"meditation"],[16.1,0.263,"peace"],[16.375,0.588,"immediately"],[16.975,0.425,"follows"],[17.413,0.9,"renunciation"]]},{"layout":"story","headline":"Who is dear to Me","visual":["Hates no creature, is friendly and compassionate","Free from \"I\" and \"mine\", forgiving, content","Not disturbed by others, and disturbs no one"],"L":["L4"],"say":"The last part of the chapter is a portrait of the devotee God loves. One who hates no creature, who is friendly and compassionate, free from I and mine, even-minded in pain and pleasure, and forgiving. One by whom the world is not disturbed, and who is not disturbed by the world. Again and again, Krishna says: such a devotee is dear to me.","start":111.168,"at":111.744,"end":134.664,"words":[[0.138,0.1,"The"],[0.25,0.35,"last"],[0.613,0.25,"part"],[0.